{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he gave him a tithe of all.</b> Abraham did not want to take for himself so much as a thread or a sandal strap, but the portion of the Most High he set apart to give to the priest. And the king of Sodom went out to meet Abraham at the Valley of Shaveh to honor him, and walked with him as far as Salem, where Melchizedek brought out bread and wine for the people who were with him. And the king of Sodom did not ask him for anything, but when he saw his generosity and righteousness — that he had given the tithe — then he too asked for the persons, by way of charity. And Abraham trusted in his Elohim that He would give him wealth and possessions and honor, and he did not want to take anything from him, and he offered to return to him all the property of Sodom — which was rightfully his — and all the property of Amorah, to restore it to its owners. For in everything he asked of him for the persons, and in everything his claim was that they should not say, 'They made Abram rich.' And the rest of the places mentioned — they struck them with the sword and did not take from the cities of the kings; only the property of Sodom and Amorah, because since their kings were lost, their cities remained abandoned. And it is possible that this is what he meant: 'If from a thread to a sandal strap' — there will remain in my hand from all the property that comes to me from all of you, 'and if I take from all that is yours' — from the property that you yourself give me."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:22.042548959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}